    "result_text": "There's only one test class in the project, and it passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe create audit line in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` now also logs `membershipLevel` and `membershipNumber` alongside the fields it already recorded (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`).\n\n**Change made** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n\nMoved the `auditLogger.info(...)` call to after the `OwnerDto` is built (and after `householdSize` is set), then sourced the two new values from the DTO's `getMembershipLevel()` / `getMembershipNumber()`. Those DTO fields are the mapper-derived values (`OwnerMapper.formatMembershipLevel` / `formatMembershipNumber`), so the logged values match exactly what the fetch endpoint returns \u2014 which is what the acceptance test compares against.\n\nThe ordering matters: `membershipLevel` depends on `membershipPoints`, which factors in `householdSize`, so the audit line is emitted only after `setHouseholdSize` and the mapping, keeping it consistent with the fetched owner.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
