    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is minimal, additive, and idiomatic:\n\n- It extends the existing single audit-log statement in place rather than introducing a new logging site or a parallel mechanism \u2014 the audit logging pattern (inline `auditLogger.info` in the controller) was already established, and this change simply follows it.\n- Moving the log statement to after `ownerDto` construction is necessary and correct in placement: the two new fields (`membershipLevel`, `membershipNumber`) live on the DTO, so the log must run once the DTO exists. Reading `id`/`customerCode`/`registrationDate` from `owner` and the membership fields from `ownerDto` is dictated by where those values reside, not an arbitrary mixing of sources.\n- No duplication is introduced, no method or class is turned into a catch-all, and the format string / argument order stay consistent with the prior line.\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find this a natural, localized extension of the existing audit line.",
